    {
      "id": "nodes",
      "title": "A line, a box",
      "plain": "Each module carries a comment line that says what it is. The tool reads those lines and draws one box for each.",
      "technical": "system-map.mjs --write reads each `@system node <id> \"<title>\" layer=<layer>` line into a node of diagrams/system-map.json; the layer is its row.",
      "focus": ["code", "annotations", "map"],
      "flows": ["declare"],
      "ms": 3600
    },
    {
      "id": "calls",
      "title": "A line, an arrow",
      "plain": "A second kind of line says whom a module calls. Each one becomes an arrow, and the map is saved in the repo beside the code.",
      "technical": "Each `@system calls <id> \"<label>\"` line is an edge from the module that owns the file. The map is committed, and the check prints 0 warning and exits 0.",
      "focus": ["annotations", "map", "checker"],
      "flows": ["connect"],
      "ms": 3600
    },
    {
      "id": "drift",
      "title": "The code moves on",
      "plain": "Later, someone has Cart read from Stock. The code now calls something the diagram does not show.",
      "technical": "A new import in cart/index.mjs crosses into stock/ with no `@system calls stock` line, so the committed map is quietly out of date.",
      "focus": ["code", "imports"],
      "flows": [],
      "ms": 3200
    },
    {
      "id": "check",
      "title": "The check says so",
      "plain": "The check compares the diagram with what the code really imports. It finds the missing arrow, and fails.",
      "technical": "checkImports resolves every import to the node that owns it: UNDECLARED_IMPORT at cart/index.mjs:4, exit 1. Run by the Stop hook as the turn ends, by diagrams-sync, or in CI.",
      "focus": ["imports", "checker", "map"],
      "flows": ["crosscheck"],
      "ms": 3800
    },
    {
      "id": "level",
      "title": "Brought level",
      "plain": "One comment line declares the call. The map file is written again, the arrow appears, and the check passes.",
      "technical": "`@system calls stock` goes in above the import; --write regenerates diagrams/system-map.json (one edge, five lines) for the same commit, and exits 0.",
      "focus": ["annotations", "checker", "map"],
      "flows": ["rewrite"],
      "ms": 4000
    },
